{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394523-titled-commoners-question","id":1394523,"title":"Titled Commoners question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-06T01:34:05-07:00","id":1394523,"title":"Titled Commoners question","content":"What kiths make for the best nobles outside the Sidhe? I have a chronicle set in the Interregnum and I need to create some NPC changeling nobles. So I need to fill that role without using the Sidhe.<br /> <br /> Is it possible for fae who aren't changelings to serve in that role? If so, what would they be? Would they just be pure chimerical creatures, or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T02:18:40-07:00","id":1394528,"title":"","content":"Well Oba and Merfolk are also born Nobles, as are the Noble caste of Menehune.<br /> <br /> But I like Dragonkin, and Ifrit as always having a dot of title. And Balor recognizes Selkies as Noble because of their descent from Balors line. And if in Arcadia proper Trolls were said to be Lords until they lost to the Sidhe and stepped down, I think this is mythically representing the gods usurping the titans.<br /> <br /> But many Fae I can see having regions Kings and Queens like the Clarauchans, Selkies, Trolls and Knockers, and even Pookah Animal Kings like Lions.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve asked about non Changeling Nobles and people often said they never tried it. But personally I think their is a lot of potential for fun in having a Gallain, Adhene, Inanimae or even Chimera as a King or Queen. Imagine during the Resurgence a Rocktroll besting Troll Lord in a duel and becoming their Jarl. Or the Firbholg who are used to being worshipped as gods saving a freehold and being worshipped as a god by the mortals nearby and an immortal queen by the Fae. How about a Glome who counsels many generations of Kings being given the title of Duke of the Mountains. Or a Chimerical God or Dragon ruling the wilderness nearby the local court, or their own Dreamrealm?<br /> <br /> Lots of fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T16:41:05-07:00","id":1394658,"title":"","content":"While many changelings have some sort of internal system of status or ranking, as far as outsiders becoming noble the most common seem to be those such as the Boggans, Eshu, Satyrs, and Trolls.<br /> <br /> Boggans, particularly for the western kithain, maintained many of the freehold communes that filled the world as commoner changelings cleaved together for survival and this history of leadership combined with their inherent social dedication as well as their natural inclination towards polite society. They make great servants and lords alike.<br /> <br /> The Eshu are proud and many do consider themselves to be ennobled, even though amongst many of the western kiths they are seen simply as nomadic outsiders. The Eshu do however claim divine ancestry and nobility, which is acknowledged in others at times.<br /> <br /> The Satyrs are also mentioned as being particularly capable to become noble commoners, although most often amongst Graybeards. The elder satyrs tend to be scholarly and wise as well as being acquainted with leadership after years of guiding tragos.<br /> <br /> The trolls are probably the main rivals of Boggans and Sidhe for the most common kith to be ennobled. As they uphold ideas of duty, honor, and pride; they are seen as trustworthy and strong leaders and many changelings would trust a troll with their lives.<br /> <br /> There are also Autumn Sidhe to mention in the C20 timeline although they are most commonly representatives of Houses Liam and Scathach, although there are also mentioned to be scattered remnants of others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T17:44:45-07:00","id":1394674,"title":"","content":"Shining Host I think comments on this with Pooka, Trolls and Eshu being the most common followed by a smattering of other kiths. But honestly I'd say Nobles should fit the area rather than trying to do some sort of statstical analysis.. if you're going to be say running a Freehold that Goes heavy on the Greek Myths you're going to have more Satyr nobles.. something that pushes more Viking more Trolls and so on..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T04:26:17-07:00","id":1394751,"title":"","content":"Trolls are an obvious choice, since they were allegedly nobles at some point before the Sidhe conquered them. Their devotion to honor and duty would allow them to serve as fine leaders, who might actually be highly resistant to corruption.<br /> <br /> Eshu could utilize their wanderlust to become leaders of the freehold's border patrol, as well as investing resources to secure and maintain the various trods that run throughout the territory. Since they're always on the move, it would be hard to sneak past their security perimeter, and they'd probably be very keen on ensuring the roads are in good condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa","name":"NewNyrufa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T04:09:18-07:00","id":1396846,"title":"","content":"In Nobles: The Shining Host, it was mentioned that in terms of political power (in terms of seats/delegates) held by Kith in the Parliament of Dreams, 42% of the seats went to the Sidhe (remember, they represent about 5% of Kithain society), with Boggans in second-place at 14% of power, and Trolls in third at 9%. Nockers were at 4th place at 8% of seats, presumably because the weight of the Bes Din allows them the ability to negotiate for political concessions.<br /> <br /> As far as ennobled commoners, I ended up having to cap them in my game due to their relative popularity in-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T22:34:03-07:00","id":1397239,"title":"","content":"Besides nobles, what about commoner knights or the equivalent of aristocratic warriors? Same makeup as the actual titled nobles? Or any differences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T22:46:08-07:00","id":1397242,"title":"","content":"I think that Fool's Luck does mention with its discussion of Commoner Court's that the commoners do tend to rally around leaders within their community who offer or work closely with warriors who can provide martial aid and protection to the community.<br /> <br /> With the return of the Sidhe, the question of Commoner Knights is still something that has to be handled delicately given both the commoner and noble divides as well as the various political impulses of the nobility. Squiring or knighting from the commoner kiths does create a means of access for those changelings to rise in rank but it also threatens the Sidhe Monopoly Over Violence.<br /> <br /> On the flip side of this question you have the warrior of the interrgenum who didn't necessarily ever acquire formal titles but earned respect and glory for their services. Boggans defending communes, eshu wandering duelists, nocker ironmongers, redcaps, satyr tragos guards, autumn sidhe knights and &quot;knights&quot;, slaugh assassins, and; of course - Trolls.<br /> <br /> Every commoner community would seek out and prize members who could defend them and they would have longstanding respect and even in the modern age, those heroes of the people are still highly honored by the common changeling and for every Lancelot of the Sidhe, the commoners will have their own Robin Hood...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T23:21:13-07:00","id":1397900,"title":"","content":"I have found that Sluagh make fun Eiluned and Ailil.<br /> <br /> My understanding is that prior to 1969, various local lords ruled, some trying to hold on to the old ways of the nobility while others adapted new forms, but outside of Scathatch and a few die hard loyalists none of them claimed to be representing the Houses as we know them. As far as the &quot;Steward of Gondor&quot; archetype, Trolls and Boggins work well for it. Trolls, Redcaps and Nockers do the Tyrant Lord role well, and Satyr, Eshu and Boggins work as the Friendly/Charismatic Patriarch/Matriarch.<br /> <br /> I think it is/was possible for Enchanted to gain court rank, but can't recall specifics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T02:44:02-07:00","id":1397934,"title":"","content":"Think in older editions who could have titles was a bit more liberal. In C20 Players Guide they do point out Chimera can't have Titles or own Freeholds, which has me snapping my fingers because it would be hella cool to have a Chimerical Dragon being a Count, or a Queen having Chimerical Suits of Armor as Knight Bodyguards. It seems like it would be fun to have Enchanted or Kinain as Squires, Pages and eventual Knights.<br /> <br /> With C20 it seems a lot of Titles like Dukes and Counts were in new Kithain Territories like Australia and some just took the Title and others had the Title and belonged to houses.<br /> <br /> It seems natural to develop a House Concordia to unite a large minority of Ennobled Commoners, and a House Discordia to unite and Ennoble Commoners discontent with the old Guard and Classic houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T12:50:20-07:00","id":1398044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394523-titled-commoners-question?p=1397934#post1397934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In C20 Players Guide they do point out Chimera can't have Titles or own Freeholds, which has me snapping my fingers because it would be hella cool to have a Chimerical Dragon being a Count, or a Queen having Chimerical Suits of Armor as Knight Bodyguards. It seems like it would be fun to have Enchanted or Kinain as Squires, Pages and eventual Knights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the Fae are divided into many different types - Kithain, Gallain, Thallain, Inanimae, Chimera and more - it is kind of silly to say only one group get to be titled. I think I'll ignore that.<br /> <br /> I think many of the mechanics in Changeling were well done, but I am of mixed minds about the actual setting. I think they did some things great, many things well, and botched up many others. If it weren't for that some of my players are big fans of Changeling and have expectations that Fae meet canon, I'd throw out most of it and reimagine the whole thing to better reflect how actual folklore view the faerie and their ongoing departure of our world. Instead, I am trying to keep the canonical bones while presenting things more as I see them.<br /> <br /> I am also considering now whether to have some of the high nobles be Lost Ones who are Sidhe. I think in their state, they can't actually govern so it'd be more like an absentee landlord and their realms have descended into anarchy, but they'd still be present, still have their titles, but there'd be increasing debate on whether they should be considered to have abdicated, and who can legitimately replace them?<br /> <br /> Not all nobles would be this. But I think having some of them be Lost Ones might be a good element to use. What do people think?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T13:44:14-07:00","id":1398055,"title":"","content":"I have long believed that having the Sidhe go away and only come back during Hippytime was a horrible mistake, and not just because I wanted to play one in Sun King France, early Hollywood, and Victorian Britain. I remember someone once pointing out that (prior to the Reckoning) every major or dynamic event in the setting had happened 20+ years ago, and nothing was really going on <i>now</i>. Combined with a pseudo feudalist political set up that lacked any of the conflicts or nuances of real feudalism, this lead to a very static setting. IMO the Sidhe should have never left at all or the return should have just started happening right before the game so that it was a main event of the setting, having them as antagonists in the main book and then doing a Sidhe Nobles and loyalists Players Guide similar to Vampires Sabbat and Mages Technocracy. <br /> <br /> As for Lost Ones, it should work fine. There can always be a Steward claiming to govern in her name or something. Or the Lost One could be perpetually in and out of Bedlam. Likewise some sort of Chimera or Bygone dragon (or devil that looks like The Darkness from Legend), an art deco Inanimae queen inspired by Metropolis, or an Enchanted Thomas Rhymer type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T22:42:23-07:00","id":1398126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394523-titled-commoners-question?p=1398055#post1398055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have long believed that having the Sidhe go away and only come back during Hippytime was a horrible mistake, and not just because I wanted to play one in Sun King France, early Hollywood, and Victorian Britain. I remember someone once pointing out that (prior to the Reckoning) every major or dynamic event in the setting had happened 20+ years ago, and nothing was really going on <i>now</i>. Combined with a pseudo feudalist political set up that lacked any of the conflicts or nuances of real feudalism, this lead to a very static setting. IMO the Sidhe should have never left at all or the return should have just started happening right before the game so that it was a main event of the setting, having them as antagonists in the main book and then doing a Sidhe Nobles and loyalists Players Guide similar to Vampires Sabbat and Mages Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. That is one the issues I have as well. I don't think the Sidhe leaving and then returning in 1969 leads to anything. And while I understand in theory why the Moon Landing is associated with wonder, that it somehow affected the Fae never made sense to me.<br /> <br /> To me, the big thing about the Fae is that they are a dying people. This was a major theme in the Enchanted World books I read when growing up so it always stuck with me. And any modern take of faerie that I liked used the same. The Hellboy comics dealt with this theme very well. I think it would have benefited Changeling to do the same. No resurgence, just an ongoing decline with a few false Indian Summers. If I didn't have a player who cooked up a background that partially involved the Sidhe not being present during this time period, I'd just have the Sidhe there.<br /> <br /> There are a few more major elements of the setting I think was mistaken, but this is certainly one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Lost Ones, it should work fine. There can always be a Steward claiming to govern in her name or something. Or the Lost One could be perpetually in and out of Bedlam. Likewise some sort of Chimera or Bygone dragon (or devil that looks like The Darkness from Legend), an art deco Inanimae queen inspired by Metropolis, or an Enchanted Thomas Rhymer type. </div> </div> </div>Alright, you convinced me to do what I wanted to do anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T23:08:30-07:00","id":1398130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394523-titled-commoners-question?p=1398126#post1398126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, the big thing about the Fae is that they are a dying people. This was a major theme in the Enchanted World books I read when growing up so it always stuck with me. And any modern take of faerie that I liked used the same. The Hellboy comics dealt with this theme very well. I think it would have benefited Changeling to do the same. No resurgence, just an ongoing decline with a few false Indian Summers. </div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is something they share with Werewolf, with both having one foot in a mythic lost past and the other in a modern world that has no place for them (even if one is doing it in the vein of Howard's inevitable passing of what passes for civilization and the other is doing it as Tolkien's decline of the elves once the age of men starts), and is probably one of the better places to start building potential crossovers from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T16:44:10-07:00","id":1398255,"title":"","content":"I wanna start off by saying that I definitely agree with other posters here that the concept of an alternate setting for CtD where the Sidhe never left earth is an interesting one that is rife with opportunities.<br /> <br /> (I also think that a recent Sidhe Resurgence setting is an interesting idea but that's probably another post)<br /> <br /> It would definitely create a more natural progression of changeling history as the commoners and sidhe alike had to endure the progression of human history and the encroachment of the World's Autumn and the coming Winter. It also compliments for me a concept that always stuck with me when I heard it, that apparently certain folklore establishes that the fair folk often resemble just-so-slightly-out-of-date human culture.<br /> <br /> So like mentioned above having Sidhe in the court of the sun king, Victorian England, or the Roaring 20s would be incredibly fun and interesting for concepts. I also agree how it might better serve to illustrate the romantic/gothic idea that the golden age has past us by that perhaps the Resurgence of canon undercuts somewhat.<br /> <br /> I agree that this would definitely be a fun idea for a setting shard or an Alt-WoD concept, although on the other hand - to be Balor's Advocate - I do think that the current canon approach has some distinct advantages.<br /> <br /> For one thing, I think it helps to justify in-setting the medieval aesthetics of changeling society. If western changelings had been living alongside humanity for the past 600 years, they would probably have bypassed fuedalism (with the history of commoners in the Interregnum saying as much) and the sidhe would have adapted to modern dreams of leadership - mayors, politicians, executives, etc.<br /> <br /> However by having the distinctly medieval Arcadian Sidhe return in the near-past of the CtD setting we can have the whimsical hybrid of modernity and medieval-aesthetic high fantasy that we do. Aside from motifs though and visual presentations of mood, I think it brings a strong theme into play.<br /> <br /> The Sidhe-Nobility of CtD play their archetypical role in the setting allegory as 'The Out-of-Touch Elite' to the T. They maintain supreme authority, they centralize resources and power, and they very much become emblematic of the sort of 1% attitudes/activities that (imo) they are meant to critique. While I acknowledge this theme could have also been presented with modern sidhe, I think that having them literally be throw-backs to a feudal age definitely illustrates a point while also serving the western fantasy motifs and visual theme.<br /> <br /> (Also this isn't to say that I think the Arcadian Sidhe can only be used as caricatures or antagonists, I think they're very interesting and some of my fave CtD characters have been Sidhe. They can *also* represent the noble ideals of a lost time, the forgotten romance of chivalry, the duty of our leaders to stand amongst us and battle on behalf of our safety and security; etc. I simply meant to illustrate that as part of their role as a setting element in a Gothic-Punk setting, they are definitely allegorical for elements of real world elitism and privelage)<br /> <br /> All of that said though, I do enjoy both approaches to the concepts of CtD and I distinctly like both settings, I simply wanted to write this post to illustrate what I view as some of the definite merits of CtD's approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T17:02:42-07:00","id":1398259,"title":"","content":"I never thought of any of this. Thanks.<br /> <br /> I hate how CtD has basically been in suspended animation since High King David was kidnapped. I mean, yes, he came back, but it\u2019s still basically like having no king at all. The setting just feels really static, like nothing interesting or important has happened in a really long time, which is the opposite of how a faerie kingdom should feel.<br /> <br /> Do you guys agree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T17:05:29-07:00","id":1398261,"title":"","content":"I was disappointed cause I read Kingdom of Willows before I read C20 and I really wanted some of the plot lines to be resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T19:41:17-07:00","id":1398276,"title":"","content":"I believe that there's a scenario in Time of Judgment that detailed how those plot threads would resolve if nobody intervenes. It was bleak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T22:06:41-07:00","id":1398289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394523-titled-commoners-question?p=1398259#post1398259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never thought of any of this. Thanks.<br /> <br /> I hate how CtD has basically been in suspended animation since High King David was kidnapped. I mean, yes, he came back, but it\u2019s still basically like having no king at all. The setting just feels really static, like nothing interesting or important has happened in a really long time, which is the opposite of how a faerie kingdom should feel.<br /> <br /> Do you guys agree?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Everyline could use a BJD type book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T00:38:04-07:00","id":1398301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394523-titled-commoners-question?p=1398259#post1398259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never thought of any of this. Thanks.<br /> <br /> I hate how CtD has basically been in suspended animation since High King David was kidnapped. I mean, yes, he came back, but it\u2019s still basically like having no king at all. The setting just feels really static, like nothing interesting or important has happened in a really long time, which is the opposite of how a faerie kingdom should feel.<br /> <br /> Do you guys agree?</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it serves little purpose to have King David return as a Barmy ol' fool. In my setting he died and Caliburn left to search for a new King.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T04:32:02-07:00","id":1398326,"title":"","content":"@Lian totally agree<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> I love that idea! What about that Lleu guy? Or is he compromised because of his thing with Faerilyth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T04:33:35-07:00","id":1398327,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> yeah, but I don\u2019t wanna end the setting. I want to continue it. Make it more vibrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T15:22:32-07:00","id":1398446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394523-titled-commoners-question?p=1398255#post1398255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one thing, I think it helps to justify in-setting the medieval aesthetics of changeling society. If western changelings had been living alongside humanity for the past 600 years, they would probably have bypassed fuedalism (with the history of commoners in the Interregnum saying as much) and the sidhe would have adapted to modern dreams of leadership - mayors, politicians, executives, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some might have, but when dealing with things like the Dreaming and magic, sometimes old forms and titles carry with them a certain amount of inherent power. This is especially true when various oaths of fealty or the like are backed up and enforced by the Dreaming. Even modern urban politics retain a certain degree of feudal nature about them (what with special interest groups, ward bosses, and families of influence) in spite of the best efforts of technocrats over the past 150 years.<br /> One of the reasons I wish Changeling's political structure was more reflective of how actual medieval feudalism worked is because a city where the local Duke or Prince or whatever has to carefully balance the needs and wants of the local Redcap gang warlord, the Nocker/Boggin working class guild alliance, the city's &quot;voodoo queen&quot;, the Childlings' Court, the Knight Commander of the Order of the Oaken Shield, The Ladies of Grace Adieu Tea Society, the Satyr Bishop of Dionysus, and the Troll march lord is much more dynamic and interesting than one where its just &quot;The Duke of the State of Ohio says I'm the Baron of Cincinnati so you all have to do what I say because that's what the rank chart says.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T18:18:20-07:00","id":1398484,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> totally agree","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T20:02:11-07:00","id":1398511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394523-titled-commoners-question?p=1398446#post1398446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some might have, but when dealing with things like the Dreaming and magic, sometimes old forms and titles carry with them a certain amount of inherent power. This is especially true when various oaths of fealty or the like are backed up and enforced by the Dreaming. Even modern urban politics retain a certain degree of feudal nature about them (what with special interest groups, ward bosses, and families of influence) in spite of the best efforts of technocrats over the past 150 years.<br /> One of the reasons I wish Changeling's political structure was more reflective of how actual medieval feudalism worked is because a city where the local Duke or Prince or whatever has to carefully balance the needs and wants of the local Redcap gang warlord, the Nocker/Boggin working class guild alliance, the city's &quot;voodoo queen&quot;, the Childlings' Court, the Knight Commander of the Order of the Oaken Shield, The Ladies of Grace Adieu Tea Society, the Satyr Bishop of Dionysus, and the Troll march lord is much more dynamic and interesting than one where its just &quot;The Duke of the State of Ohio says I'm the Baron of Cincinnati so you all have to do what I say because that's what the rank chart says.&quot;<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I would like more of this. Though I don't think all Lower Rank Nobles had to obey anyone of Higher Rank, I think it was each Noble had Vassals of Lower Ranks that directly obeyed them and tithed to them. With Some Titled Sidhe having no land or Vassals tied to their rank like Duke Guile. But I would like to have it more like your described method, which frankly is how the Kingdom of Seasons is described in the Player's Guide. I would have certain territories that are vassals only to the High King and some who are part of the local hierarchy. And some full blown secessionists joined to a House Discordia. <br /> <br /> But I like the idea a lot of the Dukes have Titles tied to Areas that only exist in the Dreaming, like the Lake of Nimue or the Murkewoods.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394523-titled-commoners-question?p=1398326#post1398326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Lian totally agree</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394523-titled-commoners-question?p=1398326#post1398326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> I love that idea! What about that Lleu guy? Or is he compromised because of his thing with Faerilyth?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In my setting a Number of the most storied Treasures from Legend have chosen new wielders in preparation for the coming winter, several of them were lost or hidden in the mists of time since the age of Legends but some were in the possession of notable changelings but left to find more worthy heirs. They bring to them the skein of destined mortals and make them one off Kiths, called Chosen, embodying their legend. So in this Case Caliburn goes to find a worthy Mortal to make into the new High King, just as Mjolnir Goes to find a Mortal to command the Thunder and Lighting but also Jarngreipr and Meginjord also each go to find someone to inherit a portion of divine might. The Thallain of the Chosen are the Accursed, those chosen by infamous and demonic items, they have a greater resonance with Urban Legends, like Freddy Krueger's Glove, and Jason's Mask or even Jack the Ripper's Knife, but also truly ancient and potent Items like the Eye of Balor becoming a Glass Eye looking for an Eyeless Mortal to make the new General of the Thallain.<br /> <br /> But if I was doing a game without that kith, I would have a young Changeling, probably but not guaranteed to be a Sidhe. Seif Raushan seems to be a fit herald for the Sword, rather then the next High King, so I may have him discover King David as he dies or have him brought back to Concordia as his fae half fades and he becomes Mortal. But Depending on when I would have David Die Lleu could be a good choice, but if David Dies closer to the modern date I would have a young Sidhe from the 2nd Resurgence chosen, as the Sword wants a new young Lord who will grow into a King rather then an established Sidhe. Lleu seems to be a mix of the Lleu from the Gwydion Myth, which was the Welsh version of Lugh but in Changeling they state Gwydion was a descendant of Lugh rather than the Uncle of Lugh, and Lancelot with probably a greater emphasis on Lancelot. People say David is a reincarnation of the Dream of Arthur Pendragon, but actually his predecessor High King Defyll might actually have been Arthur's Dream and David may have been just a Young Sidhe, or perhaps a reincarnation of Gwydion himself. Lleu would be the champion of the Realm, the Lancelot, Seif would be perhaps a new Galahad (not the dream of Galahad but the role of Galahad), and we could use a new Merlin as well, Duke Guile could be a cool fit.<br /> <br /> It could be interesting if David actually made Lenore his heir because Caliburn guided him, and it could find her in her time of need when her position is being usurped. I was always confused why so many Sidhe are children of other Sidhe... does that mean some of the Sidhe host like magiced themselves in suspensions waiting for the first wave to have children to enter into during pregnancy or do they flat out just boot out the souls of other Sidhe's kids.</span></span></span></div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T20:24:46-07:00","id":1398516,"title":"","content":"I have this image in my head of a teenaged Satyr band geek finding themselves the new holder of Pan's Pipes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-0